# examples/tempus/: the time register -- one DeModFrame carrying a node's
# held time onto the Punctim wire, and the read of one that arrives -- driven
# by its probatio.exsc.
#
# THE UNIT IS FOUR FILES, in this order: §14 entry 23's fixture (the
# DeModFrame declaration, spec §5.2 verbatim), entry 23's codex (the codec
# certified against all 246 vendored vectors), the register, the driver. The
# register restates nothing about the wire; the codec it calls is the one the
# conformance suite certifies.
#
# expected.out is WRITTEN BY prototypes/tempus_oracle.py -- struct.pack, a
# table-driven CRC, Punctim's unwrap formula -- not by this program:
#   python3 prototypes/tempus_oracle.py --wire vendor/hydramesh-wire/golden_vectors.json \
#       tests/programs/tempus/expected.out
# and `--wire` checks the oracle's own CRC against every encode-basis vector
# and the anchors before it writes anything.
#
# The exit status is the program's own check that it SEALS two published
# frames from their fields: golden_vectors.json's exampleFrame_full (10 on a
# mismatch) and the frame HydraModem's transmitter renders (11).
#
# cross=yes: the same bytes from the C backend's mips64-none-o64 row.
TEST: expect-exit=0 sources=tests/conformance/entry23_demodframe_golden_vectors.exsc,tests/conformance/entry23/codex.exsc,examples/tempus/tempus.exsc,examples/tempus/probatio.exsc cross=yes
